{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01MWtkR4PRhEKSP7tnympT1Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Project State Summary\n\n**Problem**: Classic Unix utilities lack formal specifications. This project derives specs from C source, generates Go implementations via AI, and verifies parity through differential testing against GNU reference binaries.\n\n**Architecture**: Four-stage pipeline (extract → specify → synthesize → verify). Key components: `cmd/` (utility implementations), `pkg/sys/` (syscall wrappers), `pkg/format/` (output formatting), `pkg/testutils/` (differential testing harness), `magefiles/` (build infrastructure, scaffolded externally).\n\n**Current state**: Source code exists for `pkg/testutils`, `pkg/sys`, `pkg/format`, `cmd/wc`, `cmd/cat`, `cmd/sponge`, `cmd/du`. All of releases 01.0–01.3 have generated code. Release 02.0+ specs are pending (no PRDs).\n\n**Current release**: rel00.0 (foundational infrastructure). The `pkg/` packages and `cmd/` utilities have implementations, but `pkg/format/color.go` has no corresponding test file — `columns_test.go` and `size_test.go` exist but `color_test.go` does not, leaving prd003-format R2 untested.\n\n## Priority Reasoning\n\nRelease 00.0 is the earliest release. Within it, `pkg/format` (uc002-format) has implementation code for R1 (columns), R2 (color), and R3 (size), but only R1 and R3 have test files. Adding tests for R2 (color output) completes the test coverage for this package. This is the highest-priority gap I can fill with full requirement traceability, since the source code for `color.go` is available with explicit PRD anchors in its comments.\n\n```yaml\n- index: 0\n  title: \"Add unit tests for pkg/format color output (prd003-format R2.1, R2.2, R2.3, R2.4, R2.6, R2.7)\"\n  dependency: -1\n  description: |\n    deliverable_type: code\n\n    required_reading:\n      - pkg/format/color.go (ANSI color implementation to test)\n      - docs/specs/product-requirements/prd003-format.yaml (color output requirements R2)\n      - pkg/format/columns_test.go (table-driven test pattern reference)\n      - pkg/format/size_test.go (table-driven test pattern reference)\n      - pkg/sys/terminal.go (IsTerminal used by ColorEnabled)\n\n    files:\n      - path: pkg/format/color_test.go\n        action: create\n        note: Unit tests for FileTypeColor, Reset, ColorEnabled, SetColorEnabled, ResetColorEnabled\n\n    requirements:\n      - id: R1\n        text: \"Test FileTypeColor returns correct ANSI escape sequences for each file type category (directory, symlink, executable regular file, block device, character device, socket, named pipe, non-executable regular file) when color is force-enabled via SetColorEnabled(true), per prd003-format R2.1, R2.4.\"\n      - id: R2\n        text: \"Test Reset returns the ANSI reset sequence when color is enabled and an empty string when color is disabled, per prd003-format R2.2.\"\n      - id: R3\n        text: \"Test ColorEnabled returns false for non-TTY writers (os.Pipe read/write ends, regular files) and returns false when the writer is not an *os.File, per prd003-format R2.3.\"\n      - id: R4\n        text: \"Test SetColorEnabled(true) forces color on regardless of TTY state, SetColorEnabled(false) forces color off, and ResetColorEnabled reverts to automatic TTY detection, per prd003-format R2.6, R2.7.\"\n\n    design_decisions:\n      - id: D1\n        text: \"Use SetColorEnabled(true) and SetColorEnabled(false) to control color state deterministically in tests, avoiding TTY dependency. Call ResetColorEnabled in t.Cleanup to prevent test pollution across subtests, per prd003-format R2.6, R2.7.\"\n      - id: D2\n        text: \"Follow the table-driven test pattern established in columns_test.go and size_test.go -- each test function uses a []struct with name, input, and expected fields, iterating with t.Run.\"\n      - id: D3\n        text: \"Test FileTypeColor using os.FileMode constants (os.ModeDir, os.ModeSymlink, os.ModeDevice, os.ModeCharDevice, os.ModeSocket, os.ModeNamedPipe) combined with permission bits (0o111) for executable detection, matching the switch cases in fileTypeCode.\"\n\n    acceptance_criteria:\n      - id: AC1\n        text: \"pkg/format/color_test.go exists and compiles without errors.\"\n      - id: AC2\n        text: \"go test ./pkg/format/... passes with all new color tests passing.\"\n      - id: AC3\n        text: \"Tests cover FileTypeColor for all 8 file type categories: directory, symlink, executable regular, block device, character device, socket, named pipe, and non-executable regular file.\"\n      - id: AC4\n        text: \"Tests verify that SetColorEnabled overrides automatic detection and ResetColorEnabled reverts to automatic behavior.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":80650,"cache_read_input_tokens":19289,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":80650},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9aaabb2a-a81d-4488-aa4c-42657a8247e1","uuid":"6bd11458-5479-4b00-b1d6-1b78cfa2c026"}
